   "key": "f1",
   "kind": "statement",
   "basis": "read",
   "text": "Cruelty is defined by the absence of mercy, stated explicitly, not implied. Three of H0394's six verses use the near-identical formula cruel and have no mercy (Jer 6:23, 50:42) or merciless (Jer 30:14); Prov 12:10 makes the same point as a paradox, the mercy of the wicked is cruel, that is, even their gentlest disposition still qualifies as cruelty. Cruelty here is not a separate vice alongside mercilessness; the texts treat the two as the same fact stated twice.",
